{
  "acceptance": [
    "Corpus validation rejects completed throughput bundles when len(stream_results) differs from integer run.streams, or config.streams when run.streams is absent; absent configured counts skip the check. The error names the bundle path and both counts. Failed and partial phases with truncated results do not hard-fail corpus validation solely for the count mismatch.",
    "Explorer pipeline and local result import withhold Throughput@Size when a completed phase's configured count differs from stream_results length; pipeline entries use stream_count_mismatch when the primary exclusion would otherwise be missing_primary_metric. Failed and partial phases retain the phase-failure exclusion instead of being relabeled as a count mismatch.",
    "Unit tests cover matching counts, absent configured counts, run.streams/config.streams mismatches, and failed/partial truncation across corpus validation and Explorer ranking/import behavior."
  ],
  "context": "Resume notes 2026-10-11: item4 PR #2898 merged at 11:28:26Z (merge commit fdb6ab774f16bb89c1f16c36fb3eb7dab16ff6f9), and its decision artifact is verified on origin/develop. Item5 PR #2894 was rebased onto origin/develop 2e74dc9e8; head bff6c95c6364d0aacba17186a96289cdabe6c093. Earlier Oracle D1/D2 were fixed and their threads resolved. Active `oracle-verdict.yml` dispatch 38162906528 posted a current-head SHIP WITH FIXES review with D3: completed throughput count mismatches did not exclude non-TPC geomean-ranked Explorer rows because the reason override only handled `missing_primary_metric`. Added `reason is None` handling to both manifest/detail transformer paths and a regression test for SSB/ClickBench proving the invalid row is unranked while a valid peer ranks. Targeted Python suite: 330 passed; latest `make pr-preflight`: 478 tests passed and Ruff passed; ci-docs passed; duplicate-check-delta +0; Explorer Vitest 27 passed (no TS changes). The new commit `fix: exclude stream-count mismatches from rankings` is currently running the local commit hooks. PR auto-merge remains disabled. Local `make comment-policy-check` and hosted CI 38162387383 comment-policy gate failed on 10 enforced CP coverage findings in unchanged upstream files (publication workflows, concurrency_sweep.sh, compile-all-platforms.sh, make_timing_shell.sh, release_cut_abort.sh); none are in this PR diff. After the commit completes, confirm current base, push it, update PR description, allow Oracle and CI to evaluate the new head, resolve any new addressed findings, and only arm after successful current-head Oracle and all required CI. Do not edit unrelated comment-policy paths. Then monitor merge, verify develop, finish item5, and start item6.",
